.TH rc-keeper-start 1  "rc-keeper-start " 
.SH NAME
rc\-keeper\-start \- Start an instance, or all with \-\-all
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrc\-keeper\-start\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start an instance, or all with \-\-all
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Apply to every instance. Give either this or a selector, not both
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Kills the other claude remote\-control in the folder (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 5 s), then starts. Destructive. Not with \-\-all
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt for \-\-force. Required when no terminal is attached
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISELECTOR\fR]
Instance id or folder path. Give either this or `\-\-all`, not both. An id wins when a folder path and an id match
